<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Henrique Paiva Couceiro</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1861">1861</a>–<a href="/years/1944">1944</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Henrique Paiva Couceiro was a Portuguese army officer and colonial administrator, governor-general of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/angola">Angola</a> from 1907 to 1909, and the leading royalist opponent of the First Portuguese Republic. He led royalist incursions from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> in 1911 and 1912, and on 19 January 1919 proclaimed the Monarchy of the North in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/porto">Porto</a>. Republican forces ended it within a month, and he went into exile.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/henrique-paiva-couceiro.jpg" alt="Henrique Paiva Couceiro" width="320" height="488" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Paiva_Couceiro,_President_da_Junta.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
